# Exceptions for scripts/public_check.py (rule: AGENTS.md "Public safety").
# One entry per line, each with its reason after '#':
#   <path glob>   # reason     covers every hit in the matching files
#   <path>:<line> # reason     covers the hits on that line only
#   commit:<full sha> author|committer  # reason
#                              covers the identity hits of that role on that commit only, for
#                              history already published; the same identity elsewhere still fails
#   commit:<full sha> message  # reason
#                              covers the message hits (tracker references included) of that
#                              commit only, for history already published; the same text in any
#                              other commit still fails
# File entries never cover commit messages. An entry that matches no hit fails a check that has the
# private deny list, naming its line and form, so stale exceptions cannot hide a later leak; a
# commit entry counts only in the gate of a range that holds its commit, which alone sees its hits.
